course: dictionary
lesson: 6888
title: Oversleep
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: To oversleep means to sleep longer than you meant to, so you wake up late. The prefix over- often means too much or too far, so oversleep means sleeping too far past the time you meant to wake.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Next morning Toad oversleeps again and finds only egg-shells, cold leathery toast and a coffee-pot three-quarters empty.» The word again tells you this has happened before, and the cold toast shows that breakfast was waiting while Toad slept on.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in: «Toad sleeps too long again.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning. Oversleeping can make you late for school, which is why it matters.
fact: Oversleep means to sleep longer than you meant to, so that you wake up late.
fact: The verb changes its form: oversleep, oversleeps, overslept, oversleeping. For the past, use «overslept»: «I overslept this morning.»
fact: In the story, «Toad oversleeps again» and finds cold toast and an empty coffee-pot in his own house.
fact: Frère Jacques is a French song about a monk who has overslept: «dormez-vous?» means «are you sleeping?», and in the English version the bells are already ringing.
fact: The prefix over- often means too much or too far, as in overflow, overcook and overeat.
exercise: «Next morning Toad oversleeps again.» What does oversleeps mean? | Wakes up early and feels fresh | *Sleeps longer than he meant to and wakes late | Eats too much toast | Walks down to the river
exercise: Which sentence uses the past tense of oversleep correctly? | *Yesterday I overslept and missed the bus. | Yesterday I oversleep and missed the bus. | Yesterday I oversleeps and missed the bus. | Yesterday I oversleeping and missed the bus.
exercise: In Frère Jacques the bells are already ringing, and the monk has overslept. What does this tell you? | He is awake early and ready to pray | *He has slept past the morning and is late | He is still asleep at midnight | He is out walking in the fields
test: What is the best meaning of oversleep? | To wake up before the sun rises | To sleep in a tent outside | *To sleep too long and wake late | To go to bed very early
test: Which word has the prefix over- meaning too much or too far? | *overcook | table | bake | cook
exam: Mia says, «I overslept and was late for school.» What does overslept mean? | *Slept longer than she meant and woke late | Did not sleep at all | Slept very well all night | Slept in a bed of leaves
